-- title:
--   Level raising at q preserves θ̄-corner components
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N,q$ (both nonzero) with $q$ prime and $q\nmid N$. For a level $M$ and $H\le(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$, [`CohCarrier.H1 M H A`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L162) is the group of additive homomorphisms from the additivisation of $\Gamma_H(M)$ to $A$; here $H=\top$ throughout, so the group is $\Gamma_0(M)$. Three witnesses of the predicate [`CohCarrier.LevelLE`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L330) are assumed, for $d=1$, $d=q$ and $d=q^2$, each asserting $N\mid Nq^2$, $d\mid (Nq^2)/N$ and the (vacuous, for $\top$) compatibility of the unit subgroups; each supplies the degeneracy map [`CohCarrier.iDegL`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L401) $\colon H^1(\Gamma_0(N),\mathcal O)\to H^1(\Gamma_0(Nq^2),\mathcal O)$, pull-back along the injection $\begin{pmatrix}a&b\\c&e\end{pmatrix}\mapsto\begin{pmatrix}a&bd\\c/d&e\end{pmatrix}$ of $\Gamma_0(Nq^2)$ into $\Gamma_0(N)$. Further data: a set $S$ of naturals with $q\in S$; a commutative local ring $\mathcal O$ with residue field $k$; hypotheses `hcomm`, `hcomm'` that the operator families [`CohCarrier.opFamily`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) at levels $N$ and $Nq^2$ (sending `T ℓ` and `U ℓ` to the transfer-defined operator [`CohCarrier.heckeTL`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L23) at $\ell$, and `dia d` to the conjugation operator) commute pairwise; systems of eigenvalues $\bar\theta$, $\bar\theta'$ in $k$ on the generator types at the two levels, linked by $\bar\theta'(T_\ell)=\bar\theta(T_\ell)$ for $\ell$ prime with $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid Nq^2$, by $\bar\theta'(U_\ell)=\bar\theta(U_\ell)$ for primes $\ell\mid N$, and by $\bar\theta'(U_q)=0$; idempotent splittings `Sp`, `Sp'` (complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$ together with all maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_i$, with $e_i\in\mathfrak m_j$ iff $i\ne j$) of the $\mathcal O$-subalgebras generated by the operators at the two levels, with chosen indices $i_0$, $i_0'$ and $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $\pi_k$, $\pi_k'$ from the corresponding corner rings to $k$ carrying the class of each generator operator to $\bar\theta$, respectively $\bar\theta'$, of that generator. The conclusion: if $\varphi\in H^1(\Gamma_0(N),\mathcal O)$ lies in the corner submodule $e_{i_0}\cdot H^1(\Gamma_0(N),\mathcal O)$, then $\big(q\,\iota_1^*-\iota_q^*\circ T_q+\iota_{q^2}^*\big)(\varphi)$ lies in the corner submodule $e_{i_0'}\cdot H^1(\Gamma_0(Nq^2),\mathcal O)$.
--
--   This is the raising half of the level-raising step at a prime $q$ exactly dividing the new level to the second power, as in Wiles's chain-of-levels construction; classically the combination $q\,\iota_1^*-\iota_q^*T_q+\iota_{q^2}^*$ sends a $T_q$-eigenform $f$ with eigenvalue $a_q$ to the old vector $f(\tau)-a_qf(q\tau)+qf(q^2\tau)$ annihilated by $U_q$. The formal statement is purely about the degree-one cohomology of $\Gamma_0$ as a module over the $\mathcal O$-algebra generated by the listed Hecke and diamond operators, and it asserts only the stability of corner (idempotent) components attached to an abstractly given idempotent splitting and to compatible residual eigenvalue systems with $\bar\theta'(U_q)=0$; no Galois representation, no multiplicity one and no identification of the corner rings with localised Hecke algebras enters. It is used in the construction of level-raising rungs for the Hecke-algebra realisation of a residual eigensystem, where the new level is $Nq^2$.
-- source:
